{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>She shall bear her iniquity.</b> If she became defiled." "And the meaning of <b>and the man shall be clear of iniquity</b>: for if a spirit of jealousy has passed over him, she is forbidden to him to lie with, and he who lies with her has iniquity. Some say that the reason for the juxtaposition of the passage of the nazirite to the passage of the sota is that she shall have a nazirite son if she was not defiled, and in my opinion it is juxtaposed because of the naziriteship of the woman, which is the opposite of her who acts unfaithfully, for most transgressions, their cause is wine, and a woman who does not tame the hair of her head does not seek to be lain with [i.e., does not seek sexual relations]."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:29.060045530Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}